      "title": "Three clocks protect different decisions",
      "narration": "Elena receives a new life policy, later misses a premium, and eventually faces a claim question. Those events do not start the same clock. A return or free-look period gives the owner an opportunity to review and cancel under the applicable notice. A grace period permits late payment of a premium after the first while coverage continues under its terms. An incontestability provision limits a later challenge to the policy's validity after the required lifetime period. Identify the event and the purpose before choosing a number. A familiar thirty-day answer can be wrong for the question actually asked.",
