      "title": "Incontestability limits validity challenges",
      "narration": "Maryland's standard individual-life provision makes the policy incontestable, except for nonpayment of premiums, after it has been in force during the insured's lifetime for two years after issue. The lifetime requirement matters. Death eighteen months after issue does not satisfy it merely because a claim is submitted later. During the applicable contestable period, a misstatement can require review under Maryland's materiality and other statutory tests. After the specified period, distinguish an attempted validity challenge from a defense based on a genuine coverage restriction. Incontestability is a particular contractual protection, not a promise that every event must be covered.",
