      "title": "Solve the event before doing the arithmetic",
      "narration": "Elena's policy has been in force during her lifetime for three years. Assume no separate coverage exclusion applies. She dies during its valid premium grace period, with a five hundred dollar premium overdue and a stated one hundred thousand dollar benefit. The insurer cannot simply call the policy lapsed on the missed due date when grace still protects it. Apply the permitted overdue-premium deduction, producing ninety-nine thousand five hundred dollars in this example. A proposed challenge to the original policy's validity is a different issue governed by incontestability. Keep payment status, coverage scope and validity in separate steps.",
